  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 218 AM CDT Wed May 27 2026\n\nA somewhat active weather pattern will persist through much of \nthe long term with a persistent weak upper level west-southwest \nflow with disturbances moving across our area Friday night through\nMonday. Also, a surface dryline will be located to our west late \nthis weekend and early next week. There will be moderate \ninstability and abundant moisture in the area as some lift will be\nin place Friday through Monday across the area. The severe \nweather chances look low at this time, but can rule out an \nisolated strong to marginal severe storm. Going with low to medium\nchances of rain for those days. For the remainder of the long \nterm look for mainly a dry forecast, but isolated mainly afternoon\nand evening showers and thunderstorms are possible. Expect a slow\nwarming trend with highs in the upper 80s to mid 90s by this \nweekend.",
